   "id": "svd-geometry",
   "scene": "SVDGeometrySequence",
   "section": 3,
   "title": "Turn, stretch, turn: the unit circle under $U\\Sigma V^T$",
   "summary": "For $A = \\begin{bmatrix}3&0\\\\4&5\\end{bmatrix}$: $V^T$ turns $v_1, v_2$ to the axes, $\\Sigma$ stretches by $3\\sqrt5, \\sqrt5$, $U$ turns the ellipse into place.",
   "initial": {
    "title": "Unit circle",
    "tex": "\\|x\\| = 1,\\quad v_1 = \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt2}(1, 1),\\ v_2 = \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt2}(1, -1)",
    "explanation": "The right singular vectors are marked.",
    "frame": "animations/svd-geometry/state-00.jpg"
   },
   "steps": [
    {
     "index": 1,
     "title": "Turn by $V^T$",
     "relation": "compute",
     "relationLabel": "Computation",
     "tex": "V^Tv_1 = e_1,\\qquad V^Tv_2 = e_2",
     "explanation": "The circle is unchanged; the marked vectors move to the axes.",
     "initialFrame": "animations/svd-geometry/state-00.jpg",
     "finalFrame": "animations/svd-geometry/state-01.jpg",
     "transition": {
      "src": "animations/svd-geometry/step-01.mp4",
      "duration": 1.7333,
      "frames": 52,
      "masterFrames": [
       8,
       60
      ],
      "bytes": 42867,
      "codec": "h264"
     }
    },
    {
     "index": 2,
     "title": "Stretch by $\\Sigma$",
     "relation": "compute",
     "relationLabel": "Computation",
     "tex": "\\Sigma = \\begin{bmatrix}3\\sqrt5 & 0\\\\ 0 & \\sqrt5\\end{bmatrix}",
     "explanation": "The circle becomes an ellipse with half-axes $\\sigma_1$, $\\sigma_2$.",
     "initialFrame": "animations/svd-geometry/state-01.jpg",
     "finalFrame": "animations/svd-geometry/state-02.jpg",
     "transition": {
      "src": "animations/svd-geometry/step-02.mp4",
      "duration": 1.7333,
      "frames": 52,
      "masterFrames": [
       59,
       111
      ],
      "bytes": 69850,
      "codec": "h264"
     }
    },
    {
     "index": 3,
     "title": "Turn by $U$",
     "relation": "compute",
     "relationLabel": "Computation",
     "tex": "Av_i = \\sigma_iu_i:\\quad u_1 = \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}(1, 3),\\ u_2 = \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}(3, -1)",
     "explanation": "The final ellipse is $A$ applied to the circle. Here both orthogonal factors are rotations; in general either may be a reflection.",
